Follow `RULES.md` in the repo root. Those are the last FEGE site-choking rules (v84) copied from agent `bc-a7709455-0c4d-48fe-8e9d-0c3e0f5a86b3` (Fege site choking detection_Huawei).

This repo is the NCCD zone. Use the same detection, listing, severity, chart, GeoPlot, UrgentTxBWInc, capacity-only OSS rollup, BusyHour flags, Site List 4H/1H block, and Comparison rules.

Read uploaded files from the name. `OSS` in the name means OSS KPI. `FEG` or `FEGE` in the name means the FEG port KPI (`RxMaxSpeed` is the choke trace). A physical-site or site-database name means geo, Tech, and Site Type. A thana name means the GeoPlot thana list. Dates, V1/V2, and part numbers say how to combine files. They do not change what the file is. Do not require the old Dhaka filenames.

Do not merge RARs and do not build or publish a report until the user confirms that every file has been uploaded. OSS and FEG use the same combine order, kept as separate finals: for each date, merge V1 part1+part2, merge V2 part1+part2, then merge V1+V2. Do the same for every other date. If a later upload uses a different version or part count, follow the tokens in the names. When the user confirms, score the dates in those files and keep every threshold in `RULES.md`. DHAPT35 and DHAPT48 are the shape pattern, not an NCCD name filter.

Keep the BusyHour column spelling **Chocked**. Do not use Tx Total BW to list or grade a site. Do not read the old site-level OSS RAR; roll cell-level OSS to site-hour and drop L900 (`MID(Cell Name, 8, 3)` starts with `L09`).
